<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>WES Report {{ sample_id }}</title>
<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 18mm 15mm 20mm 15mm;
    @bottom-left  { content: "Sample {{ sample_id }} · Report {{ report_id }} · Research use only"; font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7280; }
    @bottom-right { content: "Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages); font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif; font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7280; }
  }
  :root {
    --ink: #111827; --muted: #6b7280; --line: #e5e7eb; --soft: #f9fafb; --brand: #0f4c5c;
    --p: #b91c1c; --lp: #ea580c; --vus: #a16207; --lb: #2563eb; --b: #15803d;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif; font-size: 8.8pt; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.45; margin: 0; }
  h1 { font-size: 15pt; white-space: nowrap; margin: 0; color: var(--brand); letter-spacing: -0.2pt; }
  h2 { font-size: 10.5pt; color: var(--brand); margin: 16pt 0 6pt; padding-bottom: 3pt; border-bottom: 1.5pt solid var(--brand);
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.6pt; }
  h3 { font-size: 9.5pt; margin: 0 0 4pt; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  .mono { font-family: "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace; font-size: 8pt; }

  .header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; padding-bottom: 8pt; border-bottom: 3pt solid var(--brand); }
  .header .meta { text-align: right; font-size: 8pt; color: var(--muted); }
  .ruo { margin-top: 6pt; background: #fef3c7; border: 1pt solid #f59e0b; color: #78350f; padding: 4pt 8pt; font-size: 7.8pt; border-radius: 3pt; }

  .grid { display: flex; gap: 10pt; margin-top: 10pt; }
  .card { flex: 1; border: 1pt solid var(--line); border-radius: 4pt; padding: 7pt 9pt; background: var(--soft); }
  .card dt { font-size: 7.2pt; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4pt; }
  .card dd { margin: 0 0 4pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .terms span { display: inline-block; background: #e0f2f1; color: var(--brand); border-radius: 8pt; padding: 1pt 6pt; margin: 1pt 2pt 1pt 0; font-size: 7.6pt; }

  .result { margin-top: 12pt; border-left: 4pt solid var(--brand); background: #f0f7f8; padding: 8pt 10pt; }
  .result.positive { border-color: var(--p); background: #fef2f2; }
  .result.vus { border-color: var(--vus); background: #fefce8; }
  .result .headline { font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 2pt; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 4pt; }
  th { text-align: left; font-size: 7.2pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.3pt; color: var(--muted);
       border-bottom: 1pt solid var(--ink); padding: 3pt 4pt; }
  td { border-bottom: 0.5pt solid var(--line); padding: 4pt; vertical-align: top; }
  tr { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { page-break-after: avoid; }
  .keep { page-break-inside: avoid; }

  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 1.5pt 6pt; border-radius: 3pt; color: white; font-weight: bold; font-size: 7.4pt; white-space: nowrap; }
  .badge.p { background: var(--p); } .badge.lp { background: var(--lp); } .badge.vus { background: var(--vus); }
  .badge.lb { background: var(--lb); } .badge.b { background: var(--b); }
  .tier { font-size: 7pt; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .gene { font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-size: 9.5pt; }

  .variant-card { border: 1pt solid var(--line); border-radius: 4pt; padding: 8pt 10pt; margin-top: 8pt; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  .variant-card .top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; }
  .facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4pt 16pt; margin: 6pt 0; font-size: 8pt; }
  .facts b { color: var(--muted); font-weight: normal; }
  .evidence td:first-child { width: 22%; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pts { text-align: right; width: 8%; font-weight: bold; }
  .pts.neg { color: var(--b); } .pts.pos { color: var(--p); }
  .warn { margin-top: 5pt; padding: 3pt 6pt; background: #fff7ed; border-left: 3pt solid var(--lp); font-size: 7.8pt; }

  .qc { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8pt; }
  .qc .m { flex: 1 1 22%; border: 1pt solid var(--line); border-radius: 4pt; padding: 6pt 8pt; }
  .qc .v { font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; color: var(--brand); }
  .qc .l { font-size: 7.2pt; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; }

  .small { font-size: 7.8pt; }
  ul.tight { margin: 2pt 0; padding-left: 12pt; } ul.tight li { margin: 1pt 0; }
  .signoff { margin-top: 14pt; display: flex; gap: 20pt; }
  .signoff div { flex: 1; border-top: 0.8pt solid var(--ink); padding-top: 3pt; font-size: 7.6pt; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ===================== HEADER ===================== -->
<div class="header">
  <div>
    <h1>Whole Exome Sequencing Report</h1>
    <div class="muted">Germline variant analysis · phenotype-driven interpretation</div>
  </div>
  <div class="meta">
    Report ID <b>{{ report_id }}</b><br>
    Generated {{ generated }}
  </div>
</div>
<div class="ruo"><b>FOR RESEARCH AND EDUCATIONAL USE ONLY.</b> Produced by an automated pipeline that has not been clinically validated. Not for diagnostic or treatment decisions.</div>

<div class="grid">
  <dl class="card">
    <dt>Sample ID</dt><dd>{{ sample_id }}</dd>
    <dt>Sex</dt><dd>{{ sex }}</dd>
    <dt>Test</dt><dd>Whole exome sequencing (germline)</dd>
  </dl>
  <dl class="card" style="flex: 2">
    <dt>Clinical indication</dt><dd style="font-weight: normal">{{ indication or "Not provided" }}</dd>
    <dt>Phenotype (HPO terms)</dt>
    <dd class="terms">
      {% for t in patient_terms %}<span>{{ t.name }} <span class="mono" style="background:none;padding:0;margin:0">{{ t.id }}</span></span>{% else %}<span class="muted" style="background:none">None provided</span>{% endfor %}
    </dd>
  </dl>
</div>

<!-- ===================== RESULT SUMMARY ===================== -->
{% set reportable = findings.primary | selectattr("tier", "equalto", "Reportable") | list %}
{% set vus_interest = findings.primary | selectattr("tier", "equalto", "VUS of interest") | list %}
{% if reportable %}
<div class="result positive">
  <div class="headline">POSITIVE: {{ reportable | length }} pathogenic / likely pathogenic variant{{ "s" if reportable | length > 1 }} identified</div>
  In {{ reportable | map(attribute="candidate.gene") | unique | join(", ") }}, consistent with the reported phenotype and inheritance. See details below.
</div>
{% elif vus_interest %}
<div class="result vus">
  <div class="headline">UNCERTAIN: variant(s) of uncertain significance in phenotype-matched gene(s)</div>
  {{ vus_interest | map(attribute="candidate.gene") | unique | join(", ") }}: strong phenotype match and fitting inheritance, but the
  automated evidence does not reach a pathogenic classification. Expert review and additional evidence are required.
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="result">
  <div class="headline">NEGATIVE: no reportable variants identified</div>
  No pathogenic, likely pathogenic or phenotype-matched uncertain variants were found. This does not exclude a genetic cause (see Limitations).
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- ===================== PRIMARY FINDINGS ===================== -->
<h2>Primary findings</h2>
{% if findings.primary %}
<table>
  <tr><th>Gene</th><th>Variant</th><th>Zygosity</th><th>Inheritance</th><th>Classification</th><th>Phenotype match</th></tr>
  {% for f in findings.primary %}
  <tr>
    <td><span class="gene">{{ f.candidate.gene }}</span><br><span class="tier">{{ f.tier }}</span></td>
    <td><span class="mono">{{ f.variant.transcript }}</span><br>{{ f.variant.hgvsc }}<br><b>{{ f.variant.hgvsp or "" }}</b></td>
    <td>{{ f.zygosity }}</td>
    <td>{{ f.candidate.inheritance | join("/") or "?" }}<br><span class="muted small">{{ f.candidate.inheritance_fit }}</span></td>
    <td><span class="badge {{ class_css[f.variant.classification] }}">{{ f.variant.classification }}</span><br><span class="muted small">{{ f.variant.points }} points</span></td>
    <td>{{ "%.0f" | format(f.candidate.phenotype_score * 100) }}%</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">None.</p>
{% endif %}

<!-- ===================== VARIANT DETAILS ===================== -->
{% for f in findings.primary %}
{% set v = f.variant %}
<div class="variant-card">
  <div class="top">
    <h3><span class="gene">{{ f.candidate.gene }}</span> {{ v.hgvsc }} {{ v.hgvsp or "" }}</h3>
    <span class="badge {{ class_css[v.classification] }}">{{ v.classification }}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="facts">
    <span><b>Position (GRCh38)</b> {{ v.chrom }}:{{ v.pos }} {{ v.ref }}&gt;{{ v.alt }}</span>
    <span><b>Transcript</b> {{ v.transcript }}</span>
    <span><b>Consequence</b> {{ v.consequence | join(", ") | replace("_", " ") }}</span>
    <span><b>Zygosity</b> {{ f.zygosity }}</span>
    <span><b>dbSNP</b> {{ v.rsid or "-" }}</span>
    <span><b>gnomAD popmax AF</b> {{ v.popmax_af | af }}</span>
    <span><b>REVEL</b> {{ v.revel if v.revel is not none else "-" }}</span>
    <span><b>AlphaMissense</b> {{ v.am_class | replace("_", " ") or "-" }}</span>
    <span><b>ClinVar</b> {{ v.clinvar_sig | replace("_", " ") or "not reported" }}{% if v.clinvar_review %} ({{ v.clinvar_review | replace("_", " ") | replace("&", "") }}){% endif %}</span>
  </div>
  <table class="evidence">
    <tr><th>ACMG criterion</th><th>Evidence</th><th class="pts">Points</th></tr>
    {% for e in v.evidence %}
    <tr><td>{{ e.code }}</td><td>{{ e.reason }}</td><td class="pts {{ 'neg' if e.points < 0 else 'pos' }}">{{ "%+d" | format(e.points) }}</td></tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="3" class="muted">No automated criteria met.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    <tr><td></td><td style="text-align:right"><b>Total</b></td><td class="pts">{{ "%+d" | format(v.points) }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  {% if f.candidate.matched_phenotypes %}
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:4pt"><b class="muted" style="font-weight:normal">Phenotype overlap:</b>
    {{ f.candidate.matched_phenotypes | selectattr("ic", "gt", 0) | map(attribute="matched_name") | unique | join(", ") }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if v.clinvar_concordance == "discordant" %}
  <div class="warn"><b>Discordant with ClinVar:</b> ClinVar classifies this variant as <b>{{ v.clinvar_sig | replace("_", " ") }}</b> with a high review status.
    Automated criteria cannot use functional, segregation or case-level evidence. Manual review is required.</div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}

<!-- ===================== CARRIER ===================== -->
{% if findings.carrier %}
<div class="keep">
<h2>Carrier findings</h2>
<p class="small muted">Heterozygous pathogenic/likely pathogenic variants in autosomal recessive genes. Not expected to cause disease alone; relevant for reproductive counselling.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Gene</th><th>Variant</th><th>Zygosity</th><th>Classification</th></tr>
  {% for f in findings.carrier %}
  <tr><td class="gene">{{ f.candidate.gene }}</td><td>{{ f.variant.hgvsc }} {{ f.variant.hgvsp or "" }}</td><td>{{ f.zygosity }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge {{ class_css[f.variant.classification] }}">{{ f.variant.classification }}</span></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- ===================== OTHER CANDIDATES ===================== -->
{% if findings.other %}
<div class="keep">
<h2>Other ranked candidates</h2>
<p class="small muted">Next highest-ranked genes by phenotype match, variant class and inheritance fit. Listed for analyst review; not reported as findings.</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Rank</th><th>Gene</th><th>Variant</th><th>Zygosity</th><th>Class</th><th>Pheno match</th><th>Inheritance fit</th></tr>
  {% for f in findings.other %}
  <tr><td>{{ f.rank }}</td><td class="gene">{{ f.candidate.gene }}</td><td>{{ f.variant.hgvsp or f.variant.hgvsc }}</td><td>{{ f.zygosity }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge {{ class_css[f.variant.classification] }}">{{ f.variant.classification }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ "%.0f" | format(f.candidate.phenotype_score * 100) }}%</td><td class="small">{{ f.candidate.inheritance_fit }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
</div>
{% endif %}

<!-- ===================== QC ===================== -->
<h2>Sequencing quality</h2>
{% if qc %}
<div class="qc">
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ qc.mean_coverage | num }}x</div><div class="l">Mean target coverage</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ qc.pct_covered["20X"] | num if qc.pct_covered else "-" }}%</div><div class="l">Targets ≥ 20x</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ qc.pct_duplication | num(2) }}%</div><div class="l">Duplication</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(qc.read_pairs) if qc.read_pairs else "-" }}</div><div class="l">Read pairs</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(qc.snvs) if qc.snvs is defined else "-" }}</div><div class="l">PASS SNVs</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(qc.indels) if qc.indels is defined else "-" }}</div><div class="l">PASS indels</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ qc.ts_tv | num(2) }}</div><div class="l">Ts/Tv ratio</div></div>
  <div class="m"><div class="v">{{ "{:,}".format(n_variants) }}</div><div class="l">Annotated records</div></div>
</div>
{% if qc.mean_coverage is defined and qc.mean_coverage < 20 %}
<div class="warn"><b>Low coverage:</b> mean target coverage is below 20x. Variants may be missed and calls may be less reliable.</div>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p class="muted small">QC metrics not available (analysis started from a VCF).</p>
{% endif %}

<!-- ===================== METHODS ===================== -->
<h2>Methods</h2>
<div class="small">
  <p><b>Sequence analysis.</b> Reads were trimmed with fastp and aligned to GRCh38 (GATK resource bundle, ALT-aware) with BWA-MEM.
  Duplicates were marked (GATK MarkDuplicates), base qualities recalibrated (BQSR), and variants called with GATK HaplotypeCaller
  in gVCF mode over capture targets ±{{ 100 }} bp, followed by GenotypeGVCFs and GATK hard filters. Variants were normalised with bcftools.</p>
  <p><b>Annotation.</b> Ensembl VEP (cache release 116) with MANE Select transcripts, gnomAD v4.1 exome and genome allele frequencies,
  ClinVar, REVEL and AlphaMissense.</p>
  <p><b>Classification.</b> ACMG/AMP 2015 criteria with ClinGen SVI refinements, combined using the Bayesian points system
  (Tavtigian et al. 2020: Pathogenic ≥10, Likely pathogenic 6–9, VUS 0–5, Likely benign −1 to −6, Benign ≤−7).
  Automated criteria: PVS1 (LOEUF &lt; {{ thresholds.loeuf_max }}), PS1/PM5 (ClinVar), PM2_Supporting (popmax AF &lt; {{ thresholds.pm2_af }}),
  PM4, PP3/BP4 (REVEL thresholds from Pejaver et al. 2022), BA1 (&gt; {{ thresholds.ba1_af * 100 }}%), BS1 (inheritance-aware:
  {{ thresholds.bs1_af_dominant * 100 }}% dominant, {{ thresholds.bs1_af_recessive * 100 }}% recessive, {{ thresholds.bs1_af * 100 }}% otherwise), BP7.</p>
  <p><b>Phenotype prioritisation.</b> Genes were ranked by Resnik semantic similarity between the patient's HPO terms and
  HPO gene annotations, combined with variant class and fit to the gene's Mendelian inheritance mode and the observed zygosity.</p>
  <p class="muted">Resources:
    {% for k, v in resources.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.</p>
</div>

<!-- ===================== LIMITATIONS ===================== -->
<h2>Limitations</h2>
<ul class="tight small">
  <li>Exome sequencing does not reliably detect copy-number variants, structural variants, repeat expansions, deep intronic or regulatory variants, mosaicism, or variants in poorly covered or highly homologous regions.</li>
  <li>Automated classification cannot apply criteria that require case-level data (de novo status, segregation, functional studies, case-control data). Results flagged as discordant with ClinVar require expert review.</li>
  <li>Allele-frequency thresholds are generic or inheritance-based, not gene-specific (ClinGen VCEP) values. Splicing impact beyond canonical splice sites is not assessed.</li>
  <li>Phase of multiple heterozygous variants in the same gene is unknown without parental testing.</li>
  <li>Classifications reflect knowledge at the time of analysis and may change.</li>
</ul>

<div class="signoff">
  <div>Analysed by (automated pipeline) · wesinterp {{ resources.wesinterp }}</div>
  <div>Reviewed by</div>
  <div>Date</div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
